                <note rend="inline" type="source">J. C. S. Files</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Commanding General, Services of
                        Supply</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Somervell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/> C.C.S. 162/1<anchor n="1" xml:id="d411-f1"/></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Casablanca</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-01-20">January 20, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">U. S. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Aid to Russia</hi></p>
                <p>1. Existing U. S. estimates on the availability of shipping and the possibility
                    of moving troops, naval forces, supplies and equipment during 1943 allow for the
                    following U. S. sailings for Russian aid.</p>
